Cumbria Local Resilience Forum - Fenella - SITREP 8
Time of report: 15/01/2026 1800

1. SITUATION
Incident status: Major incident declared. Response phase.
Rainfall totals of 120-180 mm recorded at upland gauges.

2. SITES AND ROUTES
- Glenridding Village Hall: rest centre OPEN (run by Westmorland and Furness)
- the bridge at Pooley Bridge: CLOSED
- Cockermouth School: rest centre OPEN (run by Cumberland Council)
- Fellside: evacuated (run by Fellside Care Ltd)
- junction 40 of the M6: open with restrictions
- the Northside bridge: CLOSED
- Riverside Community Centre: operating as a rest centre (run by Cumberland Council EP team)
- Keswick School: stood down (run by Cumberland Council EP team)
- QES Kirkby Lonsdale: reopened
- West Coast Main Line (Carlisle to Lancaster): open, reduced timetable (run by Network Rail)
- A591 Keswick to Grasmere: shut, diversion in place

3. AGENCIES RESPONDING
ENW, National Highways, Cumbria Fire and Rescue Service, EA North West, North West Ambulance Service

4. NEXT MEETING
SCG at 0800. Dial-in details as previously circulated.

